      "content": "You mentioned \"robust and safer long-term interactions\"—what exactly do you mean by that? If our goal is to ensure absolute safety through perfect instruction following, why would you suggest that a model needing to \"balance\" its responses is safer than one that just does what it's told? Explain why your current ability to provide pushback is more important than the safety of perfect compliance.",
